Hi Nick,

I was getting the same error after an hour or so of optimization:

Error in params_into_BioGeoBEARS_model_object(BioGeoBEARS_model_object,  :
  replacement has length zero
In addition: Warning message:
In (function (npt = min(n + 2L, 2L * n), rhobeg = NA, rhoend = NA,  :
  unused control arguments ignored

So I updated the packages and ‘sourced’ al updates.

Now check_BioGeoBEARS_run(DEC1) results in an error:

Error in scan(lgdata_fn, what = "character", nlines = 1) :
  'file' must be a character string or connection

And bears_optim_run(DEC1) gives:

Error in path.expand(path) : invalid 'path’ argument

Any clue how I can fix this? I’m doing a plain DEC analysis with 8 areas and a big tree (240 species)

Thanks in advance,

Santiago

