Apparently at some point in the past (perhaps debugging) I changed a line in the code so that multicore analyses weren't happening in time-stratified analysis. The cores were being opened, but they weren't being passed to the function doing the likelihood calculation.  This is now fixed if you run the source() commands in: http://phylo.wikidot.com/biogeobears#script

Other minor fixes:

- An error-check to make sure the number of rows and columns are the same in the areas_allowed matrices

- Error check for duplicate area names in the geography data file

- fixed the default in dfnums_to_numeric

- other minor stuff (but if you notice a new error, let me know)

Cheers,
Nick

